 ## Background
-Local-GS was introduced to address microarchitectural limitations in the 3D Gaussian Splatting rendering pipeline, specifically poor GPU utilization due to warp divergence and redundant computation [S1, unofficial]. It shifts the optimization focus from macroscopic scene culling to microscopic GPU SIMT execution boundaries [S1, unofficial]. The method is designed as a plug-and-play acceleration module for a wide range of 3DGS frameworks [S1, unofficial].
+Local-GS was introduced in the paper "Local-GS: Accelerating 3D Gaussian Splatting via Tile-Local Warp Coherence" [S1, unofficial]. It addresses microarchitectural limitations in 3DGS rendering, specifically warp divergence and redundant computation caused by irregular spatial distribution of Gaussians [S1, unofficial]. The method shifts optimization focus from macroscopic scene culling to microscopic GPU SIMT execution boundaries [S1, unofficial].
 
